--- !u!114 &1620115408
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1620115399}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec422cd568a9c4a31ad7c36d0572b9da, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  itemId: 3
  indentLevel: 0
  storyText: That's probably what you want, if you're working on a puzzle game or
    platformer. Those tend to not be 99% story dialogue.
  description: 
  character: {fileID: 1495643923}
  portrait: {fileID: 0}
  voiceOverClip: {fileID: 0}
  showAlways: 1
  showCount: 1
  extendPrevious: 0
  fadeWhenDone: 1
  waitForClick: 1
  stopVoiceover: 1
  waitForVO: 0
  setSayDialog: {fileID: 0}
--- !u!114 &1620115409
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1620115399}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec422cd568a9c4a31ad7c36d0572b9da, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  itemId: 2
  indentLevel: 0
  storyText: You can test the functionality of the new Save System here. You can
    try to save, then load your game at any time while a Say Dialog is executing.
  description: 
  character: {fileID: 1495643923}
  portrait: {fileID: 0}
  voiceOverClip: {fileID: 0}
  showAlways: 1
  showCount: 1
  extendPrevious: 0
  fadeWhenDone: 1
  waitForClick: 1
  stopVoiceover: 1
  waitForVO: 0
  setSayDialog: {fileID: 0}
--- !u!114 &1620115412
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1620115399}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec422cd568a9c4a31ad7c36d0572b9da, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  itemId: 6
  indentLevel: 0
  storyText: Using Flowcharts, you can customize how the UI executes save-creating,
    save-loading, and save-deleting.
  description: 
  character: {fileID: 1495643923}
  portrait: {fileID: 0}
  voiceOverClip: {fileID: 0}
  showAlways: 1
  showCount: 1
  extendPrevious: 0
  fadeWhenDone: 1
  waitForClick: 1
  stopVoiceover: 1
  waitForVO: 0
  setSayDialog: {fileID: 0}
--- !u!114 &1620115413
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1620115399}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec422cd568a9c4a31ad7c36d0572b9da, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  itemId: 5
  indentLevel: 0
  storyText: Or when one isn't. In that case, no say dialogs will be brought up upon
    load, since none in this test were executing at the time you made the save.
  description: 
  character: {fileID: 1495643923}
  portrait: {fileID: 0}
  voiceOverClip: {fileID: 0}
  showAlways: 1
  showCount: 1
  extendPrevious: 0
  fadeWhenDone: 1
  waitForClick: 1
  stopVoiceover: 1
  waitForVO: 0
  setSayDialog: {fileID: 0}
